#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059469 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product Using Determinants"}] :question/id #uuid "d2698dbf-dea6-5abb-970e-a3ace180e337" :question/math-academy-id "e-4341" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3,-4,1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -7,0,2 \\rangle.$ Find $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ -7 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-4)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 0)i-(3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-7))j+(3\\cdot 0-(-4)\\cdot (-7))k \\\\  & =-8i-13j-28k \\\\  & =⟨-8,-13,-28⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059470 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/id #uuid "b834e666-de4f-5964-a280-6571ad44b6bd" :question/math-academy-id "e-4343" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3, 1, 2x \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,1,x \\rangle,$ and $|\\,\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\,| = \\sqrt{19}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2x \\\\ 0 & 1 & x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2x \\\\ 1 & x\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2x \\\\ 0 & x\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-xi-3xj+3k \\\\  & =⟨-x,-3x,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-x)^{2}+(-3x)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & |\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{19} \\\\  & \\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}=\\sqrt{19} \\\\  & 10{x}^{2}+9=19 \\\\  & 10{x}^{2}=10 \\\\  & {x}^{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x= \\pm 1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303439 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db20040e-bef4-51cd-947b-ee90d170929d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303441} {:answer/id #uuid "faedcfc3-3fa8-5c20-bf7a-c72cd7261dee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303442} {:answer/id #uuid "1b4ec3dd-346e-55d6-baa9-200d86a229b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2,4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303443} {:answer/id #uuid "f55e0fa3-387c-5657-a2fc-ea0bceb8031f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303444} {:answer/id #uuid "6daa0145-bf33-529f-bb3b-02149dfe6f9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-4,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db20040e-bef4-51cd-947b-ee90d170929d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303441} :answer-field/id #uuid "eab3d72b-5fd5-575e-b41f-09cd5ece7d50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303440}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f571d284-38ad-50ae-b89e-87bf4db6e4ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-103540" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2x,3,2⟩$, $b=⟨x,1,-1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{93}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 3 & 2 \\\\ x & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2x & 2 \\\\ x & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2x & 3 \\\\ x & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(-3-2)i-(-2x-2x)j+(2x-3x)k \\\\  & =⟨-5,-4x,x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-4x)^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+16{x}^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17{x}^{2}+25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{93} \\\\ \\sqrt{17{x}^{2}+25} & =\\sqrt{93} \\\\ 17{x}^{2}+25 & =93 \\\\ 17{x}^{2} & =68 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm 2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303446 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cca606c9-e50d-5425-957b-db71a8fabb2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3,9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303448} {:answer/id #uuid "67bd8ad0-1d67-5cfc-9ba2-2a3490c2a63a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{3},3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303449} {:answer/id #uuid "5b9b933a-4328-5b02-9c83-1bc0b01b08dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303450} {:answer/id #uuid "dbca431f-f8c5-5370-8367-5080f10591bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303451} {:answer/id #uuid "060ebcab-6b34-56bb-8d67-1f0732937168" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbca431f-f8c5-5370-8367-5080f10591bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303451} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ffd1811-7344-5aa4-a404-ef0f34a29eb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303447}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fa58a80f-ad5f-57b3-8136-8bf6f43c733c" :question/math-academy-id "q-103542" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨-1,2x,3⟩,$ $b=⟨2,-x,1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{355}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 2x & 3 \\\\ 2 & -x & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2x & 3 \\\\ -x & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2x \\\\ 2 & -x\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2x+3x)i-(-1-6)j+(x-4x)k \\\\  & =⟨5x,7,-3x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(5x)^{2}+(7)^{2}+(-3x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25{x}^{2}+49+9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34{x}^{2}+49}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{355} \\\\ \\sqrt{34{x}^{2}+49} & =\\sqrt{355} \\\\ 34{x}^{2}+49 & =355 \\\\ 34{x}^{2} & =306 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm 3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303453 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product Using Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a6e47c4-ca46-5ff6-986f-288dec76e8e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨10,-2,30⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303455} {:answer/id #uuid "7af35dae-bf7e-5d1e-b039-e796efb474eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨10,14,30⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303456} {:answer/id #uuid "a2ddde76-e3b6-5869-9055-add49dbae0a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-10,2,30⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303457} {:answer/id #uuid "6504d2f7-ce02-5a55-9a72-6b1c4afc4bf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨10,-14,30⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303458} {:answer/id #uuid "a5b3f691-7c40-51b2-ba9c-c159dfab69ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨10,2,30⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a6e47c4-ca46-5ff6-986f-288dec76e8e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨10,-2,30⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303455} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d4670d5-ec5a-5739-84d8-e9a220977f47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303454}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f2ea4789-04ff-53b9-83f0-42f591cf2261" :question/math-academy-id "q-1393" :question/problem "Let $u=⟨4,5,-1⟩$ and $v=⟨-6,0,2⟩.$ Find $u\\times v.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & 5 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ -6 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(5\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 0)i-(4\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot (-6))j+(4\\cdot 0-5\\cdot (-6))k \\\\  & =(10-0)i-(8-6)j+(0-(-30))k \\\\  & =10i-2j+30k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303460 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product Using Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c084ff9-c7b2-5468-96fa-62c7fc1ff782" :answer/type {