on.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d7d16e54-799c-5b3b-a6ad-14c29a7b216e" :question/math-academy-id "q-281969" :question/problem "Let $u=⟨3,4,-1⟩$ and $v=⟨2,-5,2⟩.$ Find $u\\times v.$\n\n$u\\times v=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(4\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot (-5))i-(3\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 2)j+(3\\cdot (-5)-4\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =(8-5)i-(6+2)j+(-15-8)k \\\\  & =3i-8j-23k \\\\  & =⟨3,-8,-23⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303482 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product Using Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55da95fb-48db-55aa-84c1-ae50d624953b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55da95fb-48db-55aa-84c1-ae50d624953b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303484} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6a0baea-8223-5d0c-b853-fa92b215af8d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303483} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c8fd702-1cfc-55e3-acfb-7c24cf8746c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303486}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c8fd702-1cfc-55e3-acfb-7c24cf8746c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303486} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac440a47-3ae6-5183-908a-7570c28ac65c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303485} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e597a2b6-0866-5603-8e49-1fdd939e2e9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303488}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e597a2b6-0866-5603-8e49-1fdd939e2e9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303488} :answer-field/id #uuid "c74251cd-df31-54bc-aa6c-b887a50d1e5c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303487}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "845eabfa-78d5-5d21-b1bb-d615704c3c3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-282146" :question/problem "Let $a=2i-7j+4k$ and $b=5i+3j-6k.$ Find $a\\times b.$\n\n$a\\times b=$\n\n{{field-1}}$\\,i\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}$\\,j\\,+\\,$\n{{field-3}}$\\,k$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -7 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-7 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & -7 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-7)(-6)-(4)(3))i-((2)(-6)-(4)(5))j+((2)(3)-(-7)(5))k \\\\  & =(42-12)i-(-12-20)j+(6+35)k \\\\  & =30\\,i+32\\,j+41\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303489 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d3c239f-a333-5d88-ae92-08380d731a45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d3c239f-a333-5d88-ae92-08380d731a45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303491} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5e8eaf8-51e0-5844-8acf-f4e6db888966" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303490} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4dcc068-e785-52f8-bc25-d5e3ae981a4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303493}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4dcc068-e785-52f8-bc25-d5e3ae981a4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303493} :answer-field/id #uuid "330de255-3b94-5b56-9e5a-f8f0c53758db" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303492}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1dba81c8-6f48-528d-b583-abc4c231bef3" :question/math-academy-id "q-282260" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2x,3,1⟩,$ $b=⟨-2x,0,4⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{280}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 3 & 1 \\\\ -2x & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2x & 1 \\\\ -2x & 4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2x & 3 \\\\ -2x & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(12-0)i-(8x+2x)j+(0+6x)k \\\\  & =⟨12,-10x,6x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{12}^{2}+(-10x)^{2}+(6x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144+100{x}^{2}+36{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{136{x}^{2}+144}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{280} \\\\ \\sqrt{136{x}^{2}+144} & =\\sqrt{280} \\\\ 136{x}^{2}+144 & =280 \\\\ 136{x}^{2} & =136 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-1,$ $x=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303494 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5155a28-22dd-54d9-904d-52eb3db422cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5155a28-22dd-54d9-904d-52eb3db422cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303496} :answer-field/id #uuid "50096657-96ad-5bc8-923d-da3a399564ce" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303495} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c56013b-cca9-556f-bfe4-7260efbe46bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303498}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c56013b-cca9-556f-bfe4-7260efbe46bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303498} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e24a0b4-61de-584c-94ac-928507f054ff" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303497}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a06a34cd-d85e-589e-9964-4d0cd1f43e22" :question/math-academy-id "q-282262" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨x,3,0⟩,$ $b=⟨-x,0,1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{49}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 3 & 0 \\\\ -x & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 0 \\\\ -x & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 3 \\\\ -x & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3-0)i-(x+0)j+(0+3x)k \\\\  & =⟨3,-x,3x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-x)^{2}+(3x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+{x}^{2}+9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\ \\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9} & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\ 10{x}^{2}+9 & =49 \\\\ 10{x}^{2} & =40 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-2,$ $x=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303499 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7220f6dc-804a-5952-8aa2-ece7984a6d00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303501} {:answer/id #uuid "05874c5d-4db0-5490-990d-5497c811900e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303502}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7220f6dc-804a-5952-8aa2-ece7984a6d00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303501} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d308653-8f1e-5f72-8077-913f2fa9da55" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303500}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e1f66b62-a151-5b00-bab4-0cd70c1a41f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-282269" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨x,1,1⟩,$ $b=⟨1,0,3⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{10}.$ Find $x.$\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3-0)i-(3x-1)j+(0-1)k \\\\  & =⟨3,1-3x,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(1-3x)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+(9{x}^{2}-6x+1)+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-6x+11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{10} \\\\ \\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-6x+11} & =\\sqrt{10} \\\\ 9{x}^{2}-6x+11 & =10 \\\\ (3x-1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ 3x-1 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{1}{3}.$"}]}
